# EduOS — environment variable NAMES only. Never put real secrets in this file,
# and never put a secret in the tracked `.env`.
#
# The tracked root `.env` is generated by the hosting platform and contains only
# PUBLIC client configuration (project id, API URL, publishable/anon key). Those
# values are shipped to every browser in the client bundle, so committing them
# discloses nothing. Anything privileged — service-role keys, payment keys and
# webhook secrets, mail credentials, signing keys — lives ONLY in the encrypted
# backend secret store and is read server-side via process.env. It must never be
# written to a file in this repository.
#
# `src/lib/__tests__/env-secret-guard.test.ts` fails the build if a tracked
# .env-style file gains a non-public key or a secret-shaped value.

# --- public client configuration (safe to commit) ---
SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-ref"
SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID="your-project-ref"
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY="sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# Optional: deployment environment marker ("production" | "staging" | "development")
# VITE_APP_ENV="development"

# --- server-only secrets: NOT stored here ---
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID, RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET, RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, LOVABLE_API_KEY, CRON_SECRET, …
# Configure these in the encrypted backend secret store only.
